      "file": "torque_limiter_torque.glb",
      "title": "Driving torque vs load torque",
      "description": "Disc springs clamp the sprocket between the friction facings. While the load torque (red) is below the set slip torque, the friction transmits the drive torque (magenta) and everything turns together. On a jam the load torque exceeds the setting: the facings slip, the hub keeps turning and the sprocket stops — protecting the drive. Tighten the nut to raise the setting.",
