  "summary": "A torque limiter protects machines from overload. In this friction type, disc springs clamp a sprocket between friction facings on a hub. Up to the set torque everything turns together; if the driven machine jams, the facings slip so the motor and gearbox are not damaged. The slip torque is set by tightening the adjusting nut.",
